<title>USA: Guest Supply Q2 sales up, net loss widens.</title>
<headline>Guest Supply Q2 sales up, net loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>MONMOUTH JUNCTION, N.J. 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>in thousands</p>
<p>						     Three Months Ended</p>
<p>							     March 31,</p>
<p>						   1997		  1996</p>
<p> Sales					 $44,287	    $37,281</p>
<p> Gross Profit				  6,923		6,634</p>
<p> Operating Income (Loss)		 (1,582)		(823)</p>
<p> Net Income (Loss)			 (1,319)		(824)</p>
<p> Earnings (Loss) per Share:	     (0.21)	     (0.13)</p>
<p> Average Shares Outstanding		6,179		6,149</p>
<p>							  Six Months Ended</p>
<p>							     March 31,</p>
<p>						   1997		  1996</p>
<p> Sales					 $91,942	    $78,995</p>
<p> Gross Profit				 17,994	     16,129</p>
<p> Operating Income				991		1,147</p>
<p> Net Income (Loss)			   (100)		  120</p>
<p> Earnings (Loss) per Share:	     (0.01)		 0.02</p>
<p> Average Shares Outstanding		6,766		6,816</p>
<p>NOTES: 1997 Q2 includes a charge of $2,187,000 for damaged, obsolete, and below standard inventory identified in the recent consolidation of the company's seven warehouses to its new distribution facility and an increase to the company's obsolescence reserve.</p>
<p>The company also had non-recurring expenses for the consolidation of $426,000, which included moving expenses, redundant rents, taxes, occupancy expenses, equipment and labor costs, and severance pay.</p>
<p>Excluding these charges, net income for the quarter would have totaled $248,000.</p>
<p>Full company name is Guest Supply Inc.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
